Focus fade-in (fovea temporal, after 0035; native/quadviews/dcsvr_twolayer_ps.hlsl, dcsvr_perception.h, dcsvr_live.h): new
key dcsvr_focus_fade_in (live, settings.cfg, 0-3 rendered frames, default 0 = off). Opaque focus (dcsvr_two_layers_alpha=3)
with a rounded focus area only. After the focus area moves, the part of it that the last rendered frames' areas did not
cover has no focus history in DLSS yet (aliased, settling over several frames) and steps from periphery to focus
resolution in one frame; on the border that showed as a flash after each landing. The focus pass now limits the
composition's fade there to rise by at most 1 / frames per rendered frame from what each of the last three frames' areas
gave the same direction (FocusFadeHistory: per eye, the focus fields of the frames before, within 200 ms), from 0.4 of
the radius outwards (full at 0.6): the middle, where a saccade lands, is never held back. The stored alpha (the ramp by
the pixel's own place) is unchanged; only the composed colour shows more periphery while the strip fades in. The
constants grow by 64 bytes (dcsvrFade, dcsvrFadeRect[3], 192 in all). Log: "DCSVR focus fade-in: ..." once when on.
